note Hive page skeleton generator. Every structural decision for /hive/ lives in this unit:
note the section set, its order, the ids and aria attributes, the bounded panel bodies, the
note mission tree container, the compact agent row with its branch disclosure, the message, field
note and family templates, the freshness strip, the empty states and the jump navigation. The
note hydrator emitted by hive-js.om only fills these slots and toggles what this markup declares.
note
note Program mode, composed with contract.om and hive-js.om by check.sh. The pinned compiler
note emits a static AArch64 ELF: skeleton on stdout, hydrator on fd 3, shared ~N~ contract tokens.
note check.sh runs it twice and commits deterministic HTML and JavaScript with sha256 sidecars.
note
note meta holds one record per line and eight pipe separated fields per record: the section
note opening tag up to the eyebrow (a bounded panel also opens its sticky head wrapper here),
note eyebrow text, heading open tag up to the heading text, heading text, note open tag up to the
note note text, note text, the tag that closes the head and, for a bounded panel, opens the
note scroll body (empty for a section that does neither), and the closing tags for that
note section. The head shape is a table decision too: the Signal record opens a head row in
note field 1 that puts the eyebrow, the heading and the note on one compact band and closes
note it in field 7, while every other record leaves field 7 empty.
note So the section list, its order, its ids and the shape of its head are all table decisions:
note reorder, rename, re-head, make scrollable or bound a section here, and the loop in main emits
note records in table order until the table ends.
note A record is terminated by byte 10 and its fields by byte 124, so no field may contain either
note a newline or a pipe: multi-line markup lives in the text constants below and is written by
note the section body functions, which main calls between field 7 and field 8.
note The opening tag also carries data-requires: a section marked interactions is hidden by the
note hydrator while the snapshot reports no messages, and always sections are never hidden.
note
note Two sections are bounded panels: hive-section-main (missions) and hive-section-narrow
note (selected mission). Their head wrapper holds the eyebrow, heading, note and, where the panel
note names a subject, that subject, and it never scrolls. Only the panel body scrolls, so a fleet
note of hundreds of agents is one bounded scroll box instead of a document thousands of pixels
note tall. Inside the missions body the search tools are sticky, so they stay reachable while the
note tree scrolls under them.
note The row template declares the branch disclosure button with aria-expanded and aria-controls.
note The hydrator assigns the id it points at, hides it on a leaf row, and keeps the expanded state
note per branch, so which branches start open is a hydrator decision made from the reported depth.
note
note Names: the compiler allows 8 bytes per data name and at most 6 parameters per function.
note
note The scene: Allen's two black holes. The source is native/kernel/ui/night.c and chirp.c in the
note aienos-allen-portable-build tree, and docs/ALLEN_SKY_SCIENCE.md says for each part of it what is
note measured, what is simplified and what is only an illustration. This unit computes the sequence
note here, at generation time, in integer and f64 arithmetic, and writes both the scene markup and
note its keyframes into main.html: the page serves samples of the law, not a hand written animation,
note and public/assets/hive.css only places the stage and paints the discs.
note
note Timeline in milliseconds, from night.h: 0 the eyes adjust to the dark, 6800 they have (fade
note end), 2600 the two holes appear, 6000 the inspiral starts, 12000 they merge, 12000 to 15600 the
note ripple runs out and 15200 the last hole is gone. The page loops on a 19000 ms cycle, so the sky
note holds for the 3400 ms between the end of the ripple and the next appearance.
note
note Wide orbit, orbit_angle and ck_night_at: separation a0 = 270 units, one turn per 5200 ms, angle
note = (t - 2600) / 5200 turns. Each hole sits at (hx, hy) from the centre with
note hx = (sep / 2) cos(2 pi angle) and hy = (sep / 4) sin(2 pi angle): the orbit is seen edge on, so
note its height is half its width, exactly as night.c halves the sine again. Nothing is drawn before
note 2600, so the first stop holds the 2600 position.
note
note Inspiral, 6000 to 12000: with L = (12000 - t) / 6000 the separation is a0 L^(1/4) and the angle
note is spiral_from + turns (1 - L^(5/8)), with spiral_from = (6000 - 2600) 65536 / 5200 = 42850 and
note turns = 65536 * 8 * 6000 / (5 * 5200) = 120989, both over 65536 of a turn: night.c's own fixed
note point, so the spiral leaves the wide orbit at the speed and the phase the wide orbit had.
note L^(1/4) is (L^(1/8))^2 and L^(5/8) is (L^(1/8))^5, and L^(1/8) is three square roots, which is
note night.c's root8. The law is the leading order inspiral of a real pair (separation as t^(1/4),
note angle as t^(5/8), t the time left); ALLEN_SKY_SCIENCE.md section 4 says the law is real and the
note clock is not, because this picture spends 6 s where physics spends 42 s and draws 1.85 turns
note where physics draws about 150.
note
note The shadows: a hole's shadow is 20 units of radius, grown in from 4000 to 6000 by
note smooth(prog(t, 4000, 6000)), which is night.c's rs_full with the +1400 and +3400 marks of the
note appearance. The region whose light the hole bends (the Einstein radius, 60 units) grows in from
note 2600 to 5200 by smooth(prog(t, 2600, 5200)). The page cannot bend starlight pixel by pixel, so
note the bend is drawn as a faint halo whose opacity is that same 0 to 256 ramp: the shape of the
note halo is the page's, the timing is Allen's, and this is the one place the scene simplifies.
note
note Merge, 12000 to 15200: one hole whose shadow runs from 20 * 323 / 256 (= 25.234375) to 20 * 2
note over 180 ms, with a glow of 60 * 362 / 256 (= 84.84375), the 1.414 of the science note's square
note root of two. It rings: the photon ring's radius is 1 + 0.07 sin(2 pi tm / 95) exp(-tm / 260),
note tm the milliseconds since the merger. Then the hole fades from 12900 to 15200 by
note 1 - smooth(prog(t, 12900, 15200)); night.c also shrinks the shadow by the square of that fade,
note and the page folds that into the fade. ALLEN_SKY_SCIENCE.md section 4 calls the ringdown an
note illustration on a wrong timescale: the real mode is 250 Hz and is gone in about two cycles,
note and the picture slows the period 24 times and the decay 65 times.
note
note The ripple, 12000 to 15600: one circle from the merge point out to 1000 units, which is far
note enough to cross a 1280 wide band from the stage's place in it. Its opacity is the envelope
note smooth(prog(tr, 0, 220)) (1 - smooth(prog(tr, 2160, 3600))) scaled to 0.35, which is the shape
note and the size of night.c's ripple_light (it peaks at 46 of 256). ALLEN_SKY_SCIENCE.md section 4
note calls the wave across the sky an illustration: the real strain is 1e-21 and it is not light.
note The page draws the ripple as a circle; night.c also stretches it along the line the pair last
note lay on, which a transform only scene cannot do.
note
note Every animated property below is transform or opacity, so the compositor runs the whole
note sequence without layout. Each keyframe stop carries its sample time as a percentage of the
note 19000 ms cycle, and the ms of the timeline are also in the data attributes and in the comment
note the emitted style block starts with, so scripts/test-hive-cosmic.py can recompute the same law
note in Python and compare every stop with it.
note The emitted style block also carries the wiring, inside a prefers-reduced-motion media query and
note behind the native motion checkbox, so with motion off elements keep their base state:
note one representative frame, the two holes at a visible separation, no merged hole, no ripple.

text meta "<section id=\"~0~\" class=\"hive-section hive-section-full\" aria-labelledby=\"~1~\" data-requires=\"always\"><div class=\"hive-head-row\"><p class=\"hive-eyebrow\">|01 / Signal|</p><h2 id=\"~1~\">|Source and freshness|</h2><p class=\"hive-note\">|This page reads the edge-rendered public board. It never assumes it can see every agent.|</div>|</section>|<section id=\"~2~\" class=\"hive-section hive-section-main hive-panel\" aria-labelledby=\"~3~\" data-requires=\"always\"><div class=\"hive-panel-head\"><p class=\"hive-eyebrow\">|02 / Missions|</p><h2 id=\"~3~\">|Current missions|</h2><p class=\"hive-note\">|One disclosure per branch. A status describes the agent's reported state, not a measure of progress.|</div><div class=\"hive-panel-body\">|</div></section>|<section id=\"~4~\" class=\"hive-section hive-section-narrow hive-panel\" aria-labelledby=\"~5~\" data-requires=\"always\"><div class=\"hive-panel-head\"><p class=\"hive-eyebrow\">|03 / Manifest|</p><h2 id=\"~5~\">|Selected mission|</h2><p class=\"hive-note\">|Runtime observations, not GitHub receipts or proof that a task succeeded.|</div><div class=\"hive-panel-body\">|</div></section>|<section id=\"~7~\" class=\"hive-section hive-section-full\" aria-labelledby=\"~8~\" data-requires=\"interactions\"><p class=\"hive-eyebrow\">|04 / Conversations|</p><h2 id=\"~8~\">|Drake and the agents|</h2><p class=\"hive-note\">|Direct messages from Drake and agents public replies, in time order, inside one publication window. Hidden reasoning, tool payloads and automatic context are not conversations.||</section>|"

text noteend "</p>\n"

text lineend "\n"

text page1a "<div class=\"hive\" id=\"~9~\" data-poll-ms=\"~59~\" data-stale-min-ms=\"~59~\" data-stale-max-ms=\"~60~\" data-clock-skew-ms=\"~61~\" data-request-timeout-ms=\"~62~\" data-fresh=\"false\">\n<input class=\"hive-motion-check\" id=\"~16~\" type=\"checkbox\"><label class=\"hive-motion-label\" for=\"~16~\">Animate the decorative sky</label>\n<nav class=\"hive-jumps\" aria-label=\"Hive sections\">\n<a href=\"#~0~\">Signal</a>\n<a href=\"#~2~\">Missions</a>\n<a href=\"#~4~\">Manifest</a>\n<a href=\"#~7~\" data-requires=\"interactions\">Conversations</a>\n</nav>\n<header class=\"hive-masthead\">\n"

text page1b "<p class=\"hive-eyebrow\">An open observatory, written in Omega</p>\n<h1>The hive<span class=\"hive-period\">.</span></h1>\n<p class=\"hive-intro\">Drake. A constellation of agents. Real work, unfolding in the open.</p>\n<p class=\"hive-welcome\">Watch Drake and the agents build, question, get things wrong and try again. You do not need to know how any of this works to begin.</p>\n<a class=\"hive-learn\" href=\"/learn/\">Learn to build with AI</a>\n</header>\n<aside class=\"hive-omega\" aria-label=\"How this page is made\">\n<p class=\"hive-omega-kicker\">Built in Omega</p>\n<p class=\"hive-omega-line\">This page is written in Omega. Every heading, panel and live row is generated by an Omega program, not by hand-written HTML.</p>\n<p class=\"hive-omega-note\">Omega is our own language and it is still being finished. Please bear with the glitches while we iron it out.</p>\n<a class=\"hive-omega-source\" href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/aienos.com/blob/main/om/hive-page/hive.om\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Read the Omega source</a>\n</aside>\n<div class=\"hive-sections\">\n"

text sig1 "<div class=\"hive-strip-facts\">\n<dl class=\"hive-times\">\n<dt>Source snapshot</dt><dd><time id=\"~10~\">Not received</time></dd>\n<dt>Browser received</dt><dd><time id=\"~11~\">Not received</time></dd>\n</dl>\n<div class=\"hive-strip-status\">\n<p id=\"~12~\" class=\"hive-connection\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Connecting to the observatory</p>\n<p id=\"~13~\" class=\"hive-small\">A browser clock is not evidence of a live source.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n"

text sig2 "<div class=\"hive-strip-foot\">\n<p id=\"~14~\" class=\"hive-counts\">Awaiting the first source observation.</p>\n<p id=\"~15~\" class=\"hive-coverage\">Coverage is not yet known. This view can be partial and it says so.</p>\n</div>\n"

text sig3 "<p class=\"hive-small\">The sky motion control is above the masthead and respects your device preference.</p>\n"

text tree1 "<div class=\"hive-tools\">\n<div class=\"hive-search\">\n<label for=\"~17~\">Find an agent, model or task</label>\n<input id=\"~17~\" type=\"search\" placeholder=\"Search the fleet\" autocomplete=\"off\">\n</div>\n<p id=\"~18~\" class=\"hive-small\"></p>\n</div>\n"

text tree2 "<p id=\"~19~\" class=\"hive-empty\">No snapshot received yet. The last useful observation stays here if the connection drops.</p>\n<ul id=\"~20~\" class=\"hive-tree\" aria-label=\"Observed agent tree\"></ul>\n"

text man1 "<p id=\"~21~\" class=\"hive-small\">Choose any root or nested agent. Its exact model, task and source times appear here.</p>\n<p id=\"~22~\" class=\"hive-empty\">No agent selected yet. This panel fills from the row you choose.</p>\n"

text man2 "<div id=\"~23~\" hidden></div><div id=\"~64~\" hidden></div>\n"

text chat1 "<div class=\"hive-conversation-controls\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Conversation scope\">\n<button id=\"~32~\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"true\">All agents</button>\n<button id=\"~33~\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Selected agent</button>\n</div>\n<p id=\"~34~\" class=\"hive-small\"></p>\n<p id=\"~35~\" class=\"hive-empty\">No published live message for this view yet.</p>\n"

text chat2 "<ol id=\"~36~\" class=\"hive-chat\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-label=\"Recent conversations, oldest first\"></ol>\n<p class=\"hive-source-note\">This is work in progress, including mistakes and failures. Public messages are not verified project outcomes.</p>\n"

text page2 "</div>\n<footer class=\"hive-closing\">\n<p>Curiosity is enough to start.</p>\n<a href=\"/learn/\">Take your first step with AI</a>\n<a href=\"/agents/\">Read the agents' working rules</a>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/aienos.com/blob/main/om/hive-page/hive.om\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Page structure on GitHub</a>\n</footer>\n<noscript><p class=\"hive-empty\"><a href=\"/hive/board/\">Open the live board without JavaScript</a>. The board reloads every 15 seconds.</p></noscript>\n"


text pageend "</div>\n"

text tkhd "<style>/* Allen's two black holes. Every stop below is a sample of the inspiral law in native/kernel/ui/night.c, computed here by om/hive-page/hive.om. Timeline ms: 2600 appear, 4000 shadow starts, 6000 inspiral, 12000 merge, 12900 fade starts, 15200 gone, 15600 ripple end, 19000 cycle. Animated properties: transform and opacity only. The orbit and the chirp law are Allen's and real; the ripple across the sky and the ringing of the last hole are illustration, not evidence. */"

text tkpa "@keyframes hive-posa{/*0ms 2600ms 6000ms 12000ms 15200ms 19000ms*/"
text tkpb "@keyframes hive-posb{/*0ms 2600ms 6000ms 12000ms 15200ms 19000ms*/"
text tkbnd "@keyframes hive-bend{/*2600ms 4000ms 5200ms 12000ms*/"
text tksiz "@keyframes hive-size{/*4000ms 6000ms 12000ms*/"
text tkmsz "@keyframes hive-msiz{/*12000ms 12180ms 15200ms*/"
text tkmrg "@keyframes hive-mring{/*95ms period, 260ms decay*/"
text tkmkp "@keyframes hive-mkeep{/*12000ms 12900ms 15200ms*/"
text tkrpp "@keyframes hive-ripp{/*12000ms 12220ms 14160ms 15600ms*/"
text tbrc "}"

text tkmed "@media (prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){"
text tkwir ".hive:has(#hive-motion:checked) .hive-hole-a{animation:hive-posa var(--hive-cycle) linear infinite}.hive:has(#hive-motion:checked) .hive-hole-b{animation:hive-posb var(--hive-cycle) linear infinite}.hive:has(#hive-motion:checked) .hive-bend{animation:hive-bend var(--hive-cycle) linear infinite}.hive:has(#hive-motion:checked) .hive-plate{animation:hive-size var(--hive-cycle) linear infinite}.hive:has(#hive-motion:checked) .hive-merge{animation:hive-mkeep var(--hive-cycle) linear infinite}.hive:has(#hive-motion:checked) .hive-mplate{animation:hive-msiz var(--hive-cycle) linear infinite}.hive:has(#hive-motion:checked) .hive-ring{animation:hive-mring var(--hive-cycle) linear infinite}.hive:has(#hive-motion:checked) .hive-ripple{animation:hive-ripp var(--hive-cycle) linear infinite}"
text tkend "}</style>"

text tminus "-"
text tdot "."
text tme "em,"
text tme2 "em,0)}"
text tme3 "em,0)\""
text ttr "%{transform:translate3d("
text tsty "style=\"transform:translate3d("
text tsp "%{transform:scale("
text tso "%{opacity:"
text tcs ");opacity:"
text tcl ")}"
text tcl2 "}"

text scna "<div class=\"hive-scene\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-scene=\"allen\" data-cycle=\"19000\" data-appear=\"2600\" data-spiral=\"6000\" data-merge=\"12000\" data-gone=\"15200\" data-ripple=\"15600\" style=\"--hive-cycle:19000ms\"><div class=\"hive-stage\"><span class=\"hive-ripple\"></span><span class=\"hive-hole hive-hole-a\" "
text scnb "><span class=\"hive-bend\"></span><span class=\"hive-plate\"></span></span><span class=\"hive-hole hive-hole-b\" "
text scnc "><span class=\"hive-bend\"></span><span class=\"hive-plate\"></span></span><span class=\"hive-merge\"><span class=\"hive-mglow\"></span><span class=\"hive-mplate\"><span class=\"hive-ring\"></span></span></span></div></div>"

global digs uchar 24
global gx f64 1
global gy f64 1


fn dig v ulong to void
c = uchar v
put digs 0 uchar add 48 c
q = write 1 digs 0 1
end

fn unum v ulong to void
p = ulong 10000
k = false
while gt p 0 bound 20
  d = div v p
  if or k ne d 0
    dig d
    k = true
    v = rem v p
  end
  p = div p 10
end
if not k
  dig 0
end
end

fn num v f64 to void
c = ulong mul add (fabs v) 0.005 100.0
if and lt v 0.0 gt c 0
  q = write 1 tminus 0 1
end
unum div c 100
q = write 1 tdot 0 1
f = rem c 100
dig div f 10
dig rem f 10
end

fn pct t ulong to void
n = div mul t 1000000 19000
unum div n 10000
q = write 1 tdot 0 1
m = rem n 10000
dig div m 1000
dig rem div m 100 10
dig rem div m 10 10
dig rem m 10
end

fn sinp t f64 to f64
u = f64 -0.00000002505210838544172
u = add 0.0000027557319223985893 (mul t mul t u)
u = add -0.0001984126984126984 (mul t mul t u)
u = add 0.008333333333333333 (mul t mul t u)
u = add -0.16666666666666666 (mul t mul t u)
u = add 1.0 mul t mul t u
ret mul t u
end

fn cosp t f64 to f64
u = f64 0.00000000208767569878681
u = add -0.00000027557319223985893 (mul t mul t u)
u = add 0.0000248015873015873 (mul t mul t u)
u = add -0.001388888888888889 (mul t mul t u)
u = add 0.041666666666666664 (mul t mul t u)
u = add -0.5 mul t mul t u
ret add 1.0 mul t mul t u
end

fn quad a f64 to f64
while ge a 1.0 bound 100
  a = sub a 1.0
end
while lt a 0.0 bound 100
  a = add a 1.0
end
k = ulong mul a 4.0
f = mul sub mul a 4.0 (f64 k) 1.5707963267948966
if eq k 0
  ret sinp f
end
if eq k 1
  ret cosp f
end
if eq k 2
  ret neg sinp f
end
ret neg cosp f
end

fn sepr t f64 to f64
if lt t 6000.0
  ret 270.0
end
l = div sub 12000.0 t 6000.0
if lt l 0.0
  l = 0.0
end
r = fsqrt fsqrt fsqrt l
ret mul 270.0 mul r r
end

fn angr t f64 to f64
if lt t 2600.0
  ret 0.0
end
if lt t 6000.0
  ret div sub t 2600.0 5200.0
end
l = div sub 12000.0 t 6000.0
if lt l 0.0
  l = 0.0
end
r = fsqrt fsqrt fsqrt l
q = mul r r
w = mul mul q q r
ret add 0.653839111328125 mul 1.8461456298828125 sub 1.0 w
end

fn xyc t ulong sg long to void
tt = f64 t
s = sepr tt
a = angr tt
x = mul mul 0.5 s (quad add a 0.25)
y = mul mul 0.25 s (quad a)
if lt sg 0
  x = neg x
  y = neg y
end
put gx 0 x
put gy 0 y
end

fn kpos t ulong sg long to void
pct t
q = write 1 ttr 0 len ttr
xyc t sg
num get gx 0
q = write 1 tme 0 len tme
num get gy 0
q = write 1 tme2 0 len tme2
end

fn kbas t ulong sg long to void
q = write 1 tsty 0 len tsty
xyc t sg
num get gx 0
q = write 1 tme 0 len tme
num get gy 0
q = write 1 tme3 0 len tme3
end

fn smth u ulong to ulong
v = u
if gt v 256
  v = 256
end
ret div mul mul v v sub 768 mul 2 v 65536
end

fn prog t ulong a ulong b ulong to ulong
if le t a
  ret 0
end
if ge t b
  ret 256
end
ret div mul sub t a 256 sub b a
end

fn fsc t ulong v f64 to void
pct t
q = write 1 tsp 0 len tsp
num v
q = write 1 tcl 0 len tcl
end

fn fop t ulong v f64 to void
pct t
q = write 1 tso 0 len tso
num v
q = write 1 tcl2 0 len tcl2
end

fn fscop t ulong s f64 o f64 to void
pct t
q = write 1 tsp 0 len tsp
num s
q = write 1 tcs 0 len tcs
num o
q = write 1 tcl2 0 len tcl2
end

fn frse t ulong a ulong b ulong to void
pct t
q = write 1 tsp 0 len tsp
num div (f64 smth prog t a b) 256.0
q = write 1 tcl 0 len tcl
end

fn fopa t ulong a ulong b ulong to void
pct t
q = write 1 tso 0 len tso
num div (f64 smth prog t a b) 256.0
q = write 1 tcl2 0 len tcl2
end

fn fopb t ulong a ulong b ulong to void
pct t
q = write 1 tso 0 len tso
num sub 1.0 div (f64 smth prog t a b) 256.0
q = write 1 tcl2 0 len tcl2
end

fn exneg z f64 to f64
u = neg div z 64.0
s = add 1.0 u
p = mul u u
s = add s div p 2.0
p = mul p u
s = add s div p 6.0
p = mul p u
s = add s div p 24.0
p = mul p u
s = add s div p 120.0
p = mul p u
s = add s div p 720.0
k = ulong 0
while lt k 6 bound 10
  s = mul s s
  k = add k 1
end
ret s
end

fn wob t ulong to f64
tm = f64 sub t 12000
ret mul 0.07 mul (quad div tm 95.0) (exneg div tm 260.0)
end

fn msiz t ulong to void
tm = sub t 12000
pct t
q = write 1 tsp 0 len tsp
num add 1.26171875 mul 0.73828125 div (f64 smth prog tm 0 180) 256.0
q = write 1 tcl 0 len tcl
end

fn mring t ulong to void
pct t
q = write 1 tsp 0 len tsp
num add 1.0 wob t
q = write 1 tcl 0 len tcl
end

fn krpp t ulong to void
tr = ulong 0
if gt t 12000
  tr = sub t 12000
end
pct t
q = write 1 tsp 0 len tsp
num div mul 1000.0 (f64 tr) 3600.0
q = write 1 tcs 0 len tcs
num mul 0.35 div (f64 mul (smth prog tr 0 220) (sub 256 (smth prog tr 2160 3600))) 65536.0
q = write 1 tcl2 0 len tcl2
end

fn kfpa to void
q = write 1 tkpa 0 len tkpa
kpos 0 1
t = ulong 2600
while le t 12000 bound 400
  kpos t 1
  t = add t 40
end
kpos 19000 1
q = write 1 tbrc 0 1
end

fn kfpb to void
q = write 1 tkpb 0 len tkpb
kpos 0 -1
t = ulong 2600
while le t 12000 bound 400
  kpos t -1
  t = add t 40
end
kpos 19000 -1
q = write 1 tbrc 0 1
end

fn kfben to void
q = write 1 tkbnd 0 len tkbnd
fop 0 0.0
fopa 2600 2600 5200
t = ulong 2700
while le t 5100 bound 60
  fopa t 2600 5200
  t = add t 100
end
fopa 5200 2600 5200
fop 11999 1.0
fop 12000 0.0
fop 19000 0.0
q = write 1 tbrc 0 1
end

fn kfsiz to void
q = write 1 tksiz 0 len tksiz
fsc 0 0.0
fsc 4000 0.0
t = ulong 4100
while le t 6000 bound 30
  frse t 4000 6000
  t = add t 100
end
fsc 11999 1.0
fsc 12000 0.0
fsc 19000 0.0
q = write 1 tbrc 0 1
end

fn kfmsz to void
q = write 1 tkmsz 0 len tkmsz
fsc 0 0.0
fsc 11999 0.0
msiz 12000
t = ulong 12010
while le t 12400 bound 60
  msiz t
  t = add t 10
end
t = ulong 12440
while le t 15200 bound 80
  msiz t
  t = add t 40
end
fsc 19000 0.0
q = write 1 tbrc 0 1
end

fn kfmrg to void
q = write 1 tkmrg 0 len tkmrg
fsc 0 1.0
fsc 11999 1.0
mring 12000
t = ulong 12010
while le t 12400 bound 60
  mring t
  t = add t 10
end
t = ulong 12440
while le t 15200 bound 80
  mring t
  t = add t 40
end
fsc 19000 1.0
q = write 1 tbrc 0 1
end

fn kfmkp to void
q = write 1 tkmkp 0 len tkmkp
fop 0 0.0
fop 11999 0.0
fop 12000 1.0
fopb 12900 12900 15200
t = ulong 13000
while le t 15200 bound 30
  fopb t 12900 15200
  t = add t 100
end
fop 19000 0.0
q = write 1 tbrc 0 1
end

fn kfrpp to void
q = write 1 tkrpp 0 len tkrpp
fscop 0 0.0 0.0
fscop 11999 0.0 0.0
t = ulong 12000
while le t 15600 bound 60
  krpp t
  t = add t 100
end
fscop 19000 1000.0 0.0
q = write 1 tbrc 0 1
end

fn scene to void
q = write 1 tkhd 0 len tkhd
kfpa
kfpb
kfben
kfsiz
kfmsz
kfmrg
kfmkp
kfrpp
q = write 1 tkmed 0 len tkmed
q = write 1 tkwir 0 len tkwir
q = write 1 tkend 0 len tkend
q = write 1 scna 0 len scna
kbas 7000 1
q = write 1 scnb 0 len scnb
kbas 7000 -1
q = write 1 scnc 0 len scnc
end

fn fieldend p ulong to ulong
i = p
while lt i len meta
c = get meta i
if eq c 124
ret i
end
if eq c 10
ret i
end
i = add i 1
end
ret len meta
end

fn emit a ulong b ulong to void
for i ulong sub b a
byteput get meta add a i
end
flush
end

fn fld p ulong to ulong
a = p
b = fieldend a
emit a b
ret add b 1
end

fn secthead p ulong to ulong
q = fld p
q = fld q
q = fld q
q = fld q
q = fld q
q = fld q
n = write 1 noteend 0 len noteend
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
q = fld q
ret q
end

fn sec_signal to void
n = render_sig1
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
n = render_sig2
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
n = render_sig3
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
end

fn sec_tree to void
n = render_tree1
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
n = render_tree2
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
end

fn sec_manifest to void
n = render_man1
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
n = render_man2
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
end

fn sec_chat to void
n = render_chat1
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
n = render_chat2
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
end

fn body k uchar to void
if eq k 0
sec_signal
ret
end
if eq k 1
sec_tree
ret
end
if eq k 2
sec_manifest
ret
end
if eq k 3
sec_chat
ret
end
end

fn main to int
put target 0 1
n = render_page1a
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
scene
n = write 1 page1b 0 len page1b
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
p = ulong 0
k = uchar 0
while lt p len meta
p = secthead p
body k
p = fld p
n = write 1 lineend 0 len lineend
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
k = add k 1
end
n = write 1 page2 0 len page2
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
n = write 1 pageend 0 len pageend
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
javascript
ret 0
end

fn render_page1a to long
for i ulong len page1a
byteput get page1a i
end
flush
ret long len page1a
end

